<article class="env-definition" id="F14D54">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F14D54">Definition <span data-tag="F14D54">8.3.2.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathbf{S}$ be a monoidal model category, and let $\calC $ be a $\mathbf{S}$-enriched category. We will say that a morphism $f$ in $\calC $ is an <em>equivalence</em> if the homotopy class $[f]$ of $f$ is an isomorphism in $\rm {h} \it {\calC }$.equivalence!in a $\mathbf{S}$-enriched category </p>
  <p>We will say that $\calC $ is <em>locally fibrant</em> if, for every pair of objects $X,Y \in \calC $, the mapping space $\bHom _{\calC }(X,Y)$ is a fibrant object of $\mathbf{S}$.fibrant!locallylocally fibrant </p>
  <p>We will say that a $\mathbf{S}$-enriched functor $F: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ is a <em>local fibration</em>fibration!local if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
For every pair of objects $X,Y \in \calC $, the induced map $\bHom _{\calC }(X,Y) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC '}(FX,FY)$ is a fibration in $\mathbf{S}$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
The induced map $\rm {h} \it {\calC } \rightarrow \rm {h} \it {\calC '}$ is a quasi-fibration of categories. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
